 "answer": "# Part A: Integers 1-12,000 divisible by 3, 5, or 7, but not by 13\n\n**Step 1: Count numbers divisible by 3, 5, or 7 (inclusion-exclusion)**\n\n- Div by 3: \u230a12000/3\u230b = 4000\n- Div by 5: \u230a12000/5\u230b = 2400\n- Div by 7: \u230a12000/7\u230b = 1714\n- Div by 15: \u230a12000/15\u230b = 800\n- Div by 21: \u230a12000/21\u230b = 571\n- Div by 35: \u230a12000/35\u230b = 342\n- Div by 105: \u230a12000/105\u230b = 114\n\nUnion = 4000+2400+1714 \u2212 800\u2212571\u2212342 + 114 = **6515**\n\n**Step 2: Subtract those also divisible by 13**\n\nCount divisible by 13 AND (3 or 5 or 7), using lcm's with 13:\n\n- 39: \u230a12000/39\u230b = 307\n- 65: \u230a12000/65\u230b = 184\n- 91: \u230a12000/91\u230b = 131\n- 195: \u230a12000/195\u230b = 61\n- 273: \u230a12000/273\u230b = 43\n- 455: \u230a12000/455\u230b = 26\n- 1365: \u230a12000/1365\u230b = 8\n\nSum = 307+184+131 \u2212 61\u221243\u221226 + 8 = **500**\n\n**Answer:** 6515 \u2212 500 = **6015**\n\n---\n\n# Part B: 86^130 mod 233 (233 is prime)\n\nUsing repeated squaring mod 233:\n\n- 86\u00b2 = 7396 \u2261 173\n- 86\u2074 = 173\u00b2 = 29929 \u2261 105\n- 86\u2078 = 105\u00b2 = 11025 \u2261 74\n- 86\u00b9\u2076 = 74\u00b2 = 5476 \u2261 117\n- 86\u00b3\u00b2 = 117\u00b2 = 13689 \u2261 175\n- 86\u2076\u2074 = 175\u00b2 = 30625 \u2261 102\n- 86\u00b9\u00b2\u2078 = 102\u00b2 = 10404 \u2261 152\n\nSince 130 = 128 + 2:\n\n86^130 \u2261 86^128 \u00b7 86^2 \u2261 152 \u00b7 173 = 26296 mod 233\n\n26296 \u2212 233\u00b7112 (=26096) = 200\n\n**Answer: 200**\n\n---\n\n# Part C: Original price\n\nCombined multiplier:\n0.9 \u00d7 1.25 \u00d7 1.12 \u00d7 1.20 \u00d7 1.20\n\n= 0.9\u00d71.25 = 1.125\n= 1.125\u00d71.12 = 1.26\n= 1.26\u00d71.20 = 1.512\n= 1.512\u00d71.20 = 1.8144\n\nSo: P \u00d7 1.8144 = 412.08\n\nP = 412.08 / 1.8144 = 42925/189 \u2248 227.1164\n\n**Answer: $227.12**\n\n---\n\nFINAL: 6015; 200; 227.12"
